#!/bin/bash
# Report-QA roadmap loop — self-paced, read REPORT_QA_SPEC.md ledger and execute first unchecked task
# Run: claude loop < QA_LOOP.sh
# Or:  cat QA_LOOP.sh | claude loop

Read REPORT_QA_SPEC.md Section 7 (TASK LEDGER) and do only the first unchecked [ ] task, following that task's spec item (P0-n/P1-n) exactly — the Bug/Fix/Acceptance text is the requirement, the ledger line is the scope. Hard rules: NEVER invent data, thresholds, or API behavior — read the actual code the ledger anchors name (deepResearchService.ts, PdfDocument.tsx, tavilyService.ts, reportQaGates.ts) before editing; every new check is a pure exported function with a unit test derived from the Section 4 regression table; reuse the existing verifier/telemetry structs — do not build parallel plumbing; no new market-ui dependencies unless already in package.json (check first); only DeepSeek is a live LLM provider and Tavily is quota-dead (432), so live end-to-end pipeline runs are BLOCKED — verify with unit tests + frozen fixtures from eval/fixtures or eval/out, and when an acceptance criterion is live-run-only (dated-source %, real PDF visual splits, judge-scored loop runs), implement + unit-test the mechanism, then ledger-note the deferred live verification honestly instead of faking it. A task is done only when: its regression tests (Section 4 numbers named in the ledger line) are green via npx vitest run, npx tsc --noEmit is 0 errors for market-ui, and nothing unrelated broke (run the existing deepResearchService.p0b/phase1 test files if you touched the pipeline). Then flip the ledger line to [x], append ONE Section 8 Progress-log line with REAL numbers (test counts, line counts — no adjectives), and commit on roadmap/world-class with message "feat(qa): QA-n <what> — <verify numbers>" (git commit -F file if the message has quotes — rtk mangles them). Never git push unless asked. PERSISTENCE: this loop must survive usage/rate limits — never end the loop because of a limit, quota, 429, or overloaded error; on any such error stop consuming tokens immediately, ScheduleWakeup at maximum delay (3600s) with this exact /loop prompt, and on wake re-read the ledger + Progress log and resume the same task from its last verified step (log partial progress BEFORE long/risky operations so the ledger is your recovery state); chain hourly wakeups as many times as needed. Only stop for: no [ ] remaining in Section 7, or a task blocked on credentials/infra only the user can provide (e.g. Tavily quota restore for live verification) — then say exactly what's needed, ledger-note it, skip to the next unblocked [ ] task if one exists, and only if ALL remaining tasks are blocked ScheduleWakeup (3600s) so the loop resumes when unblocked.
